  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4971c5eb32d68c6419c2b82ec69e3fa3, type: 3}
  m_Name: ErraticeMouseMovementTwo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NarratorEventData
  eventID: ErraticMouseMovementTwo
  dialogueLines:
  - The player is still spinning their view around. Seriously, slow down.
  - The player seems determined to look everywhere at once. This is getting ridiculous.
  - The player is whipping the camera around again. The narrator is starting to get
    annoyed.
  - Must the player look in every direction simultaneously? Please, just pick one.
  - The player is still frantically moving the camera. Enough already.
  - The player appears to be testing the limits of the camera. The narrator is not
    amused.
  - "The player is spinning around again. At this point, they\u2019re just making
    everyone dizzy."
  - The player really needs to calm down with the camera. This is becoming rather
    irritating.
  - The player is looking around wildly again. The narrator would appreciate some
    stability.
  - The player refuses to stop spinning the camera. Fine. Keep it up and see what
    happens.
  canRepeat: 1
  priority: 1
